# Cargo target directory

The command sandbox sets `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to a fresh folder under
`%TEMP%\cursor-sandbox-cache\<hash>\cargo-target` each session. Every one becomes a full
6-23 GB build, and they piled up to 48 GB and filled the disk mid-build.

Before any `cargo` command in a shell session, point it back at the project's `target/`
(gitignored, reused across sessions):

```powershell
$env:CARGO_TARGET_DIR = "$PWD\target"; $env:PATH = "$env:USERPROFILE\.cargo\bin;$env:PATH"
cargo build -p acvd-game
```

If a build fails with "not enough space on the disk", check `%TEMP%\cursor-sandbox-cache`
for leftover `cargo-target` folders before anything else.
